nded_derivative_covectors:0","e:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_derivative_covectors:conclusion:Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_derivative_covectors:0"],"kind":"dock","label":"BoundedDerivatives.bounded_derivative_covectors","nodeId":"c:Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives","semanticId":"Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_derivative_covectors"},"dock:Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_recipe_solution":{"href":"../lax-342547/Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.html#s-Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_recipe_solution","incident":["e:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_recipe_solution:conclusion:Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_recipe_solution:0"],"kind":"dock","label":"BoundedDerivatives.bounded_recipe_solution","nodeId":"c:Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives","semanticId":"Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_recipe_solution"},"dock:Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_response":{"href":"../lax-342547/Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.html#s-Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_response","incident":["e:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_recipe_solution:assumption:Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_response:0","e:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_response:conclusion:Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_response:0"],"kind":"dock","label":"BoundedDerivatives.bounded_response","nodeId":"c:Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives","semanticId":"Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_response"},"dock:Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.observed_projection":{"href":"../lax-342547/Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.html#s-Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.observed_projection","incident":["e:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.allowed_projection:assumption:Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.observed_projection:0","e:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.observed_projection:conclusion:Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.observed_projection:0"],"kind":"dock","label":"BoundedDerivatives.observed_projection","nodeId":"c:Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives","semanticId":"Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.observed_projection"},"p:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.allowed_projection":{"href":"../lax-342547/Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.allowed_projection.html","incident":["e:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.allowed_projection:assumption:Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.observed_projection:0","e:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.allowed_projection:conclusion:Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.allowed_projection:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"Observe an allowed channel vector only through its pairings with the baseline image. This observation factors through the baseline dual map. A section onto its image therefore gives a projection inside the same allowed value space with rank at most the baseline rank.","nodeId":"p:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.allowed_projection","semanticId":"Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.allowed_projection","tooltipHtml":"Observe an allowed channel vector only through its pairings with the baseline image. This observation factors through the baseline dual map. A section onto its image therefore gives a projection inside the same allowed value space with rank at most the baseline rank."},"p:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_component":{"href":"../lax-342547/Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_component.html","incident":["e:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_component:assumption:Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_derivative_covectors:0","e:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_component:conclusion:Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_component:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"Use the full combined primal spaces for both reciprocal baseline maps. Their bounded covector ranks control the two replacement derivatives. Coordinate matrix tests prove that every component response is unchanged for arbitrary input matrices.","nodeId":"p:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_component","semanticId":"Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_component","tooltipHtml":"Use the full combined primal spaces for both reciprocal baseline maps. Their bounded covector ranks control the two replacement derivatives. Coordinate matrix tests prove that every component response is unchanged for arbitrary input matrices."},"p:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_derivative":{"href":"../lax-342547/Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_derivative.html","incident":["e:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_derivative:assumption:Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.allowed_projection:0","e:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_derivative:conclusion:Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_derivative:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"Postcompose the derivative map with the allowed value projection. All observed dot products are preserved and the derivative image lies in the bounded-dimensional projection image.","nodeId":"p:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_derivative","semanticId":"Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_derivative","tooltipHtml":"Postcompose the derivative map with the allowed value projection. All observed dot products are preserved and the derivative image lies in the bounded-dimensional projection image."},"p:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_derivative_covectors":{"href":"../lax-342547/Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_derivative_covectors.html","incident":["e:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_derivative_covectors:assumption:Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_derivative:0","e:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_derivative_covectors:conclusion:Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_derivative_covectors:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"Convert baseline covectors into their coordinate vectors. Coordinate conversion cannot increase rank; apply the allowed derivative replacement to this actual observation map.","nodeId":"p:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_derivative_covectors","semanticId":"Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_derivative_covectors","tooltipHtml":"Convert baseline covectors into their coordinate vectors. Coordinate conversion cannot increase rank; apply the allowed derivative replacement to this actual observation map."},"p:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_recipe_solution":{"href":"../lax-342547/Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_recipe_solution.html","incident":["e:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_recipe_solution:assumption:Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_response:0","e:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_recipe_solution:assumption:Lax342547.ResponseSolvability:0","e:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_recipe_solution:conclusion:Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_recipe_solution:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"Start from the proved unrestricted solution of the actual scalar recipe. Replace its two derivative families with bounded-rank families while preserving the pure response and every derivative contraction. This retains the whole-space linearized solution with the paper baseline rank bound.","nodeId":"p:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_recipe_solution","semanticId":"Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_recipe_solution","tooltipHtml":"Start from the proved unrestricted solution of the actual scalar recipe. Replace its two derivative families with bounded-rank families while preserving the pure response and every derivative contraction. This retains the whole-space linearized solution with the paper baseline rank bound."},"p:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_response":{"href":"../lax-342547/Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_response.html","incident":["e:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_response:assumption:Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_component:0","e:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_response:conclusion:Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_response:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"Choose the two bounded derivatives independently in every component. The component identities preserve the full response on the actual cut-profile pair space. Both derivative ranks are at most three times the pin budget plus twenty-eight.","nodeId":"p:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_response","semanticId":"Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.bounded_response","tooltipHtml":"Choose the two bounded derivatives independently in every component. The component identities preserve the full response on the actual cut-profile pair space. Both derivative ranks are at most three times the pin budget plus twenty-eight."},"p:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.observed_projection":{"href":"../lax-342547/Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.observed_projection.html","incident":["e:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.observed_projection:conclusion:Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives.observed_projection:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"Choose a linear section of the observation map onto its range. Composing that section with the observation map preserves all observations and bounds the new image dimension by the observation rank.","nodeId":"p:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.observed_projection","semanticId":"Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.observed_projection","tooltipHtml":"Choose a linear section of the observation map onto its range. Composing that section with the observation map preserves all observations and bounds the new image dimension by the observation rank."}}},"status":"7 statements; 7 proofs","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"prepared-graph\" width=\"488\" height=\"400\" viewBox=\"0 0 488 400\" aria-label=\"Proof dependency graph\" data-layout-digest=\"788d2c5b7d274a9c4581334de98bebff7460128643d16dd76f09e28c41ebcd16\"><defs><marker id=\"graph-arrow-proof-network-788d2c5b7d274a9c-statements:Lax342547.BoundedDerivatives\" viewBox=\"0 -5 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"0\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" markerUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\" orient=\"auto\" overflow=\"visible\"><path d=\"M1,-4.25 L9,0 L1,4.25 Q3,0 1,-4.25 Z\"/></marker></defs><g data-graph-camera><path class=\"graph-edge-hit\" data-edge-hit=\"e:Lax342547Proofs.BoundedDerivatives.allowed_p